    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup efficiency is anchored today by **Cal Raleigh** (74.56), who enters a plus matchup against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez. With a 4.73 xERA opposing him, **Cal Raleigh** is our top priority, leveraging both his power profile and a favorable spot in the two-hole. Close behind in the efficiency rankings is **Tyler Freeman** (63.63); despite facing the formidable Freddy Peralta, **Tyler Freeman** benefits from a massive 14% park adjustment and high-efficiency potential against a slow-delivering pitcher, making him a sneaky play for stolen bases. **Gavin Sheets** (59.95) remains a solid start, as the matchup against Houser allows his raw power to play up in the middle of the order.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today's roster involved the bench, where **Jonathan Aranda** (47.03) narrowly missed the final slot. While **Jonathan Aranda** maintains an attractive .374 xwOBA, his efficiency score was dragged down by a negative park adjustment and a platoon disadvantage against Corbin, which tipped the scale in favor of **Matt Chapman** (47.05) and **Jeremiah Jackson** (47.33). Meanwhile, **Geraldo Perdomo** (47.47) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (55.69) face significant headwinds against aces like Paul Skenes and Cole Ragans. While **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is an auto-start due to elite pedigree, the sub-20% SP skill penalty for both players underscores the difficulty of today\u2019s pitching slate.\n\nManagement must remain vigilant regarding the pending lineup statuses for **Bryson Stott**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Lawrence Butler**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, and **Taylor Ward**. We are counting on **Bryson Stott** to exploit the slow delivery of Jeffrey Springs, but if he falls out of the lineup or if unfavorable late-breaking wind reports materialize, his marginal efficiency could drop below the start threshold. Furthermore, **Taylor Ward** and **Jeremiah Jackson** are battling thin margins against Eury P\u00e9rez; if either finds themselves lower in the batting order than projected, we will need to reconsider their utility to preserve our game caps.",
